  "statement": "\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse your calculator to find the combined area of the shaded regions in the figure for different values of the radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e. What is the least whole–number value of \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e for which the combined area of the shaded regions is greater than 100 square units?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class\u003d\"problemstatement_figure\"\u003e\n \u003cimg src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-q.gif\"\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
  "statementFigure": null,
  "question": null,
  "widgetSlot": null,
  "steps": [
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the area of the circumscribed square.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe circumscribed square (that is, the square drawn around the circle) has side length 2\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe area of a square with side length \u003ci\u003es\u003c/i\u003e units is \u003ci\u003es\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e square units.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSo, the circumscribed square has area (2\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e)\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e \u003d 4\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-1 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-q.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the area of the circle.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe area of the circle is simply \u003ci\u003eπ\u003c/i\u003e\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the area of the shaded regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe combined area of the shaded regions is the difference between the area of the square and the area of the circle.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eA\u003c/i\u003e \u003d 4\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e – \u003ci\u003eπ\u003c/i\u003e\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e2\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eEnter this function in your calculator.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19869\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qyeq.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19869\u0026quot;,265)\"\u003e to enter this function in your calculator.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFor Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e, enter \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19870\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q4.gif\"\u003e\u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19871\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qx73.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19871\u0026quot;,263)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19872\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qxsqr.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19872\u0026quot;,260)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19873\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qminus.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19873\u0026quot;,185)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19874\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19875\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qpi.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19875\u0026quot;,200)\"\u003e\u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19876\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qx73.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19876\u0026quot;,263)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19877\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qxsqr.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19877\u0026quot;,260)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-7 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-1.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19878\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19879\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtblset.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19879\u0026quot;,231)\"\u003e to change the table settings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19880\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19881\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtblset.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19881\u0026quot;,231)\"\u003e and set TblStart \u003d 1, Δ Tbl \u003d 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-9 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-2.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19882\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19883\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtable.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19883\u0026quot;,228)\"\u003e to view the table.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19884\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19885\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtable.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19885\u0026quot;,228)\"\u003e to view the table.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-11 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-3.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eScroll down until the numbers in Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e are greater than 100.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eScroll down until the numbers in Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e are greater than 100.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eWe see that the least whole number value for \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003efor which the combined area of the shaded regions is greater than 100 square units is 11.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-13 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_1_80/f-80-1-4.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
